# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# npm project configuration — read by every install, including Vercel's.
#
# Two settings, both here because they must apply no matter which command the
# platform runs or where it runs it.
#
# `include=dev`
#   Vercel installs with production-mode npm, which omits devDependencies — and
#   `vite` and `typescript` are devDependencies, correctly: they are build tools,
#   not runtime code. That omission is what produced `vite: command not found`
#   after a 95-package install.
#
#   Each service in vercel.json also passes `--include=dev` explicitly, which is
#   the primary fix and what the guard enforces. This line is deliberate
#   belt-and-braces: the failing deployment ran the *root* `npm run build`, not a
#   service build, which suggests a production install that did not come from a
#   service `installCommand` at all. Setting it here means a plain `npm ci` — from
#   the root, from a workspace, in production mode, invoked by us or by the
#   platform — still installs the build toolchain. The alternative is a build that
#   works only when it happens to be driven by one particular config path, which is
#   the failure being fixed.
#
# `cache` (not `cache-dir`)
#   Vercel's build image exports `npm_config_cache_dir`, and npm 11+ rejects that
#   as an unknown key:
#
#     npm warn Unknown env config "cache-dir". This will stop working in the next
#     major version of npm.
#
#   `cache-dir` was never an npm setting (`cache` is), so the value was never
#   honoured. It arrives from the build environment and is not ours to unset, so
#   the supported key is pinned here.
#
# Nothing else belongs here. In particular there is no `ignore-scripts`: that would
# suppress every dependency lifecycle script as a side effect and silently starve
# native packages, which is exactly what `allowScripts` in package.json exists to
# decide deliberately and per package.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
cache=~/.npm
include=dev
